            <ArticleTitle>First use of a 5 French diagnostic catheter as a guiding catheter for percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>276-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the first use of a 5 French thin-wall, large-lumen diagnostic angiographic catheter as a guiding catheter for emergency angioplasty with an angioplasty balloon on a wire (PROBE) for patients with acute circumflex coronary occlusion and hemodynamic compromise.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
